\/PolicyResponse","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/policyresponse","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"PolicyResponse","abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GET"},{"text":" response: the stored policy plus the unknown-AAGUID action it currently ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"resolves to"}]},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unknown_aaguid"},{"text":" is nullable, where ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"text":" means “use this mode’s default” (deny under","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"direct_required"},{"text":", allow otherwise). A client that only saw the stored ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"text":" would have to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"re-derive that rule itself to display what the policy actually does — and a security rule","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implemented twice is a security rule that will eventually disagree with itself. So the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"server resolves it once, here, and reports both: the admin’s stored intent and its effect."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PolicyResponse"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","kind":"symbol","title":"AxiamSDK","abstract":[{"text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management).","type":"text"}]}}}